.TH CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_REG_COUNT 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_event_loop_reg_count \- number of currently-registered ccol_event_reg handles
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

size_t ccol_event_loop_reg_count(ccol_event_loop loop);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function returns the number of live registrations, that is, of
ccol_event_loop_add() calls that nothing has removed yet, and not the
number of entries in the epoll interest list. One fd with both
directions registered counts as 2, because two independent
ccol_event_reg handles back that fd, although they share one entry.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  ccol_event_loop to query.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns the count of the registrations on success, or (size_t)-1 when
loop is CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_INVALID, or a handle that is stale or that
something already destroyed.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call at the same time as ccol_event_loop_add(), as
ccol_event_loop_remove(), and as a dispatch on any reactor thread. It
returns a consistent snapshot: a single atomic load, which cannot
tear, with no lock that protects the value.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_event_loop_add (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_remove (3)
